{
  "_id": "650000000000000000000000",
  "title": "Build a One-Bit ALU",
  "description": "An arithmetic logic unit (ALU) selects between arithmetic and logic operations. Build a one-bit ALU using A and B as data inputs, Cin as carry-in, and S1 and S0 to choose the operation.\n\nS1 S0 = 00: A AND B\nS1 S0 = 01: A OR B\nS1 S0 = 10: A XOR B\nS1 S0 = 11: A + B + Cin\n\nR is the one-bit result. For addition, Co is the carry-out: the total is R + 2 x Co. For all logic operations, ignore Cin and keep Co at 0.\n\nThis is one slice of a larger ALU: multiple slices can share the select inputs and pass carry from one slice to the next.",
  "hints": [
    "Build the AND, OR, XOR, and full-adder results in parallel. The full adder accepts A, B, and Cin.",
    "A MUX selects its first data input when select is 0 and its second when select is 1. Use S0 to choose AND versus OR in one MUX, and XOR versus sum in another.",
    "Use S1 in a third MUX to choose between those two results for R. Co should be the full-adder carry AND S1 AND S0."
  ],
